{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1777965923,"nonce":"Pmaiudi8QN6qAj0BWK04k2+gsbw=","message":"Partial work shipped on main as --ingest v2 (default).\n\nScope shift: the original M2 spec called for the chunks to BE master blocks within a real UC2 v3 archive.  That requires either a new entry type (UC2 archives have one master per file, not a chain) or a substantial refactor of compress.c's master-block path.  Multi-session work.\n\nWhat v2 (this issue) actually delivers:\n- Self-contained archive: chunk pool embedded inside the archive file, no sidecar \u003carchive\u003e.blocks/ directory.  Solves the main UX wart of v1.\n- Format change: header bumps to v=2; manifest entries grow to 16B each (8B hash + 4B length + 4B abs offset).  Backward-compatible reader for v=1 archives still works.\n- Dedup map: power-of-two cap with mask-based linear probing.  Intra-call dedup works (same hash within a stream stores chunk once).\n- Cross-archive dedup is NOT preserved.  Trade-off for the single-file UX.  Future v3 will revisit.\n\nTests: 6 cases now (was 5).  Replaced cross-call dedup test with intra-call (same-buffer-twice produces deduped chunks within one ingest).  New v2_self_contained test asserts the .blocks/ directory is absent after writing a v2 archive.\n\nClosing this as v2 shipped.  v3 (real UC2 v3 archive integration) is filed separately as the next milestone.","files":null}]}